  <!--
    1.12.251 -> 1.12.252, UNIT 296 TASK 1, UNDER HM-DEC-150. A PATCH BECAUSE THE NIGHT'S WHOLE
    PRODUCT SO FAR IS A MEASUREMENT: no file under src/ changed, and what was added is an instrument
    and the trace it took. FT4's decode rate is measured for the first time on a lattice that
    belongs to no analysis grid - twenty-five placements spanning one whole tone spacing and one
    whole symbol period, five divisions a side so that no power-of-two oversampling can turn an
    off-grid cell into an on-grid one. At -13 dB, where the on-grid rate is exactly one, the worst
    cell keeps 19 of 36 and the placement average 808 of 900; at -15 dB the worst cell keeps
    nothing. The deficit the tree had guessed at two to three decibels is measured: 3 dB at the
    worst cell and 2 dB placement-averaged. Zero wrong decodes over all 2988 slots. One slot decodes
    in 66.9 ms, which is 0.89% of a slot.
  -->
  <!--
    1.12.252 -> 1.12.253, UNIT 296 TASK 2, UNDER HM-DEC-150. A PATCH, AND THE OPERATOR CAN SEE HALF
    OF IT. Ft8Reader.NoWholeSlot read "there is not a whole fifteen-second slot in what was kept" and
    it reaches the mode strip line and the decoded summary through Ft8Heard.Refusal, so on FT4 -
    whose slot is 7.5 seconds - it named a length twice the one being cut, in the one sentence whose
    whole job is to say that nothing was cut at all. It now names no length: a const on a static
    reader cannot know which mode the audio was captured on, so 7.5 would be wrong on FT8 exactly as
    often as fifteen was wrong on FT4. Four assertions enforce it across all three refusals on the
    decode path, and the rule they enforce is the unit of time rather than the number, so the
    cutter's honest "one whole transmission" is not refused. The other half is a test file:
    TheWholeChainRunsFromOneRightClickTests's row finder asked OfType<Grid> for a row whose root has
    been a StackPanel since unit 280, which is unit 293's fix in the FT4 sibling made here. Two of
    its three tests were dying in the finder, measured by reverting; all three pass.
